# Fleet-default CODEOWNERS — installed into every gyrum-labs/* repo by
# gyrum-fleet-protection-sweep (warp#2914) and apply-fleet-branch-protection.sh.
#
# Why: the canonical branch-protection template sets
# `require_code_owner_reviews: true`. For that flag to gate merges on
# the 3-persona AI review (priya/marcus/lin per CLAUDE.md), the persona
# bot accounts MUST own paths a PR is likely to touch. The catch-all
# pattern below ensures every PR routes through a CODEOWNER review,
# and the named accounts are the persona bots that `gyrum-review-pr`
# posts approvals from.
#
# Required (count toward branch-protection's quorum):
#   gyrum-priya, gyrum-marcus, gyrum-lin
# Advisory (CLAUDE.md "advisory; gates local gyrum-review-pr only"):
#   gyrum-dana, gyrum-sasha, gyrum-quinn
#
# All six are listed because GitHub's CODEOWNERS treats every named
# owner as a potential reviewer; the 2-of-N gate is enforced by
# `required_approving_review_count: 2` in the protection template.
# Persona-recusal (warp#1392) drops a recused persona from the
# effective quorum at gyrum-review-pr time; protection-side quorum
# stays at 2 because warp-recusal already produces ≥2 remaining
# approvers in every recusal scenario the policy allows.
#
# This file is canonical for the fleet. Do NOT hand-edit per repo —
# any drift is overwritten on the next fleet sweep tick. To add a new
# persona, edit `templates/CODEOWNERS` in gyrum-labs/devtools and let
# the sweep propagate it.

